    {
      "id": "solver-quaternion-normalize-approx",
      "name": "SolverQuaternionNormalizeApprox",
      "category": "SolverBody",
      "signature": "SolverQuaternionNormalizeApprox(Target, In Out Q)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FSolverBody*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Out Q",
          "type": "FRotation3&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "@brief An approximate quaternion normalize for use in the solver\n@note we need to correctly normalize the final quaternion before pushing it back to the\nparticle otherwise some tolerance checks elsewhere will fail (Integrate)\nThis avoids the sqrt which is a massively dominating cost especially with doubles\nwhen we do not have a fast reciproical sqrt (AVX2)\nThis uses the first order Pade approximation instead of a Taylor expansion\nto get more accurate results for small quaternion deltas (i.e., where\nQ.SizeSquared() is already near 1).\nQ.Normalized ~= Q * (2 / (1 + Q.SizeSquared)))\nIn practice we can use this for almost any delta generated in collision detection\nbut we have an accurate fallback just in case. The fallback adds a branch but this\ndoes not seem to cost much."
    },
    {
      "id": "solver-quaternion-apply-angular-delta-approx",
      "name": "SolverQuaternionApplyAngularDeltaApprox",
      "category": "SolverBody",
      "signature": "SolverQuaternionApplyAngularDeltaApprox(Target, In Q 0, In DR)",
      "params": [
